Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Spindles Choke the Flywheel
- Story & Context: During a citywide substation fire that plunged the Brás textile corridor into darkness, Tiago Silva threaded thirty feet of bleached polyester film leader through the teeth of an uncalibrated Bell & Howell projector. Standing in the strobe of raw white projection light, the band tore into a two-hundred-BPM nylon-and-chug frenzy that scored a phantom documentary about automated looms devouring their operators, the acoustic guitar body taking heavy hits from Silva’s knuckles until his cuticle cracked against the bridge. The police cruiser stationed at the corner mistook the percussive acoustic clatter for machine-shop gunfire, only to find three sweaty musicians screaming through an old copper megaphone: "Feed the scrap to the teeth, let the fabric burn!"
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: High-contrast experimental film still of an antique cast-iron textile spindle jammed with shredded celluloid film strips, sparks showering over a blurred acoustic soundboard, printed on high-grain monochrome stock with splashes of faded tropical yellow ink.

Track 2: Who Left the Selvage Fraying?
- Story & Context: Written during a twenty-four-hour lockout inside Cine Marrocos, Helena Prado sat on a stack of damp burlap flour sacks, tracing an imaginary revenge melodrama about a garment stitcher sabotaging municipal power cables. Her right hand, raw from tensioning steel strings against a warped spruce top, executed a rapid-fire tropical acoustic strumming pattern that crashed against Bianca’s sub-dystopian synth drones and squealing fuzz guitars. When building security hammered on the heavy iron doors demanding silence, the band merely dialed the tape-delay feedback to maximum and let Prado’s hoarse voice cut through the mechanical grind: "I stitched my thumb into the hem so I wouldn’t float away."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Macro photography of a frayed denim jacket hem intertwined with unspooled magnetic tape and rusted guitar wire, illuminated by the harsh flare of an industrial work lamp against cracked lime-green plaster walls.

Track 3: Cine República, Unstitched
- Story & Context: The morning after an arsonist laid waste to the Cine República’s mezzanine, scavengers picking through the sodden velvet seats unearthed a charred acetate reel containing the only live tape of this legendary closer. Recorded as smoke filled the balcony, the track captures the ensemble playing at full thrash velocity against the sound of falling ceiling plaster, using syncopated acoustic batucada slaps to keep time while the celluloid melted in the gate. The myth of the performance outlived the theater itself, remembered as the night the musicians tried to stitch the burning room together with high-speed sound before howling into the soot: "Unspool the ghost before the rafters drop!"
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Surreal, cinematic illustration of a collapsed theater auditorium open to a smoggy night sky, where the theater screen is a massive quilt of charred fabric strips and unspooled film ribbons glowing with dying embers.

